# ⚠️  CRITICAL FIX: Google OAuth Client IDs
# 
# ERROR CAUSE: "Error 400: invalid_request" + "This app doesn't comply with Google's OAuth 2.0 policy"
# 
# ROOT ISSUE: GOOGLE_EXPO_CLIENT_ID and GOOGLE_WEB_CLIENT_ID are currently IDENTICAL
# This violates Google OAuth 2.0 policy which requires different client IDs for different platforms.
#
# REQUIRED FIX: Create THREE separate OAuth applications in Google Console:
# 1. Separate Expo Go client (for development)
# 2. Separate Web client (for browser)
# 3. Separate Android client (for native APK)
#
# See: docs/GOOGLE_OAUTH_SETUP.md for complete step-by-step setup instructions
# 
# After setup, replace the values below with YOUR THREE DIFFERENT client IDs
# =========================================================================

# ⚠️  MUST BE DIFFERENT from GOOGLE_WEB_CLIENT_ID below
EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_EXPO_CLIENT_ID=746795156003-g4gugahc8bp65eg91as09naprrhpq3ee.apps.googleusercontent.com

# ⚠️  MUST BE DIFFERENT from GOOGLE_EXPO_CLIENT_ID above
EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_WEB_CLIENT_ID=746795156003-g4gugahc8bp65eg91as09naprrhpq3ee.apps.googleusercontent.com

# Android native APK client (different from both above)
EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_ANDROID_CLIENT_ID=746795156003-imf0rh7q52pvmlst9i67che88pi1orpa.apps.googleusercontent.com